# Linear ↔ GitHub sync (WaveDB)

Linear project: **WaveDB** ([Linear](https://linear.app/xamantra/project/wavedb-80ca4d1f17c8)). Team key: **PER** (issues like `PER-123`).

## When starting work

- Pick or create a Linear issue in the **WaveDB** project before medium/large code changes.
- Move the issue to **In Progress** when implementation begins.
- Prefer Linear’s suggested branch name (`gitBranchName` on the issue) when working on a single issue; otherwise commit on **`dev`** per `pull-requests.mdc`.

## Pull requests (`dev` → `main`)

Every PR that implements or fixes tracked work must **link Linear in the PR body**:

```markdown
## Linear
- PER-XX — short title (https://linear.app/xamantra/issue/PER-XX/...)
```

- Use one bullet per issue when a PR spans multiple items.
- In the **Summary**, mention the issue ID(s) in plain text (e.g. “PER-7: persist engine stats across restart”).
- If the GitHub ↔ Linear integration is enabled, include a closing keyword on its own line for auto-close on merge, e.g. `Fixes PER-7` (one issue per line if multiple).

When creating or refreshing the open `dev` → `main` PR (`gh pr edit`), **preserve or add** the **Linear** section; do not drop issue links when updating title/body for new commits.

## After merge

- Confirm linked issues moved to **Done** (via integration or manually in Linear).
- If work was partial, leave the issue open and note what shipped in a Linear comment.

## Agents and automation

- Before opening/updating a PR, use Linear MCP to find the matching **WaveDB** issue; if none exists, ask whether to create one.
- When a PR URL exists, add it to the issue via **links** (attachment) or a comment so the issue shows the GitHub PR.
- Do not mark Linear issues Done until the change is merged to **`main`** (or explicitly released), unless the user asks otherwise.
